  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **LMLYP** (1 review): Reviewer calls this LMLYP insane and among the best they have seen live [3]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Back To Basum**: rare: 12 archived performances [4]\n- **Spirit Of '76**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **Push The Lil' Daisies**: back after 38 archived shows (677 days) [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **ween1999-08-06.flac16** (recommended): source not stated; 31 songs; 206 min; rated 4.5/5 by 2 [1]. Said about its sound: Recording sounds pretty good for a Ween show at the Warfield, a room where getting a good mix is tricky [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- The band played 3 hours 26 minutes, with the only real break coming before the encore [2]\n- After The Grobe the crowd cheered so loudly that Aaron remarked it would be a long night, and the band then played with fire [3]\n- Reviewer's first Ween show in San Francisco and roughly their second overall; the first featured The Poopship Destroyer, which appears on Paintin' The Town Brown [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **ween1999-08-06.flac16**: taped by Lobster; transferred by Lobster; source: Nak300 > Sony D10 Pro II [1]",
